        "text": "Supply and demand create the market and determine prices. But what exactly makes up the levels of demand and supply in a market? The amount of assets supplied for sale in a financial market has many reasons behind it. For example, the supply of gold can be affected by the amount mined, production costs and import taxes and tariffs, among other things. The overall demand in a market like gold can be affected by the state of the global economy, returns on alternative investments and other factors. Many see gold as a place to store money when there are economic problems or in an emergency. If financial markets are down and we are perhaps entering a recession, some people like to invest in gold as a safe haven, causing the demand to increase. Whether we are talking about apples in a grocery store, gold on financial markets, or cryptocurrencies, the principles of demand and supply are always the same. The only difference will be what affects supply and demand in each financial market.",
        "start": 720,
        "end": 56610,
